      <div type="commentary">
        <p n="1" ana="#tr.print">The framed manuscript page number ⲗⲃ is printed with a bar above and below as the frame, not as a supralinear stroke. ⲡⲣⲣⲟ carries no stroke (6× zoom); the only stroke on the line is over the first ⲛ of ⲛⲛⲁⲡⲕⲉⲕⲉ (822–835).</p>
        <p n="1" ana="#tr.layout">Line in ekthesis with an enlarged ⲡ.</p>
        <p n="4" ana="#tr.reading">ⲯ (arms curved up) in ⲥⲕⲉⲯⲓⲥ.</p>
        <p n="9" ana="#tr.layout">A large middle dot (·) stands after ⲛⲥⲉϫⲉ.</p>
        <p n="11" ana="#tr.print">Measured stroke over ⲙⲛ (762–782, pixel row): ⲙ 52 %, ⲛ 57 %, encoded on both. The footnote prints its lemma ⲙⲁⲕⲕⲙⲉⲕ with a dot under the second ⲕ; the text line has none (6× zoom).</p>
        <p n="14" ana="#tr.layout">Line in ekthesis with an enlarged ⲟ.</p>
        <p n="14" ana="#tr.reading">All ϣ on the page were compared at 6× (ll. 1, 7, 11, 14, 15, 16, 23, 24, 25, 27, 31); none has a separate sublinear dot.</p>
        <p n="17" ana="#tr.print">Measured stroke over ⲛϥ of ⲛϥϫⲓⲧⲟⲩ (810–827, pixel row): ⲛ 53 %, ϥ 58 %, encoded on both.</p>
        <p n="18" ana="#tr.print">The stroke over ⲗⲗ of ⲛⲟⲩⲗⲗⲟⲟⲗⲉ (1000–1022, pixel row) covers the first ⲗ 84 %, the second 16 %: encoded on the first only.</p>
